{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1367327-um-i-might-need-stats-for-a-deathlord","id":1367327,"title":"Um. I might need stats for a Deathlord.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-02-12T16:28:46-08:00","id":1367327,"title":"Um. I might need stats for a Deathlord.","content":"My players are escorting a caravan of around 800 living people out of the deep Underworld, and they've just hit the borders of lands claimed by Walker in Darkness. Encouraged by a friendly encounter with one of his Abyssal and some totally trustworthy advice they don't remember getting from the Green Lady, they decided that it would be a good idea to send about half the party ahead to visit him and pay their respects. And my over-dramatic ass decides to have him pop up right next to them while they're staring up at his fortress and wondering &quot;wait... was this a good idea?&quot; And that's where the session ended.<br /> <br /> Obviously, I'm not planning on having Walker try to murder them. He's actually pretty well-disposed towards the party right now; they've killed a couple Abyssals working for one of his main rivals and stopped a major invasion she was launching. But I can't imagine he'd pass up the chance to dribble some corruption into their ears.<br /> <br /> The players currently in his face include:<ul><li>A Presence-supernal Eclipse with a bit of medicine and Silver-Voiced Nightingale. Not so hot at mechanics.</li> <li>A Lore-supernal Twilight with a bit of Sorcery and raw strength. She's got a strong ranged attack (a variant of The Burning Name using longbow stats), but no other combat magic.</li> <li>A Dodge-supernal Night with the usual mix of Rogue-y stuff.</li> </ul><br /> So, uh... suggestions? I've never done much social encounter building before.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12314-grod_the_giant","name":"Grod_the_giant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12314_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-12T16:38:25-08:00","id":1367328,"title":"","content":"What are you running the Walker as? Like is he a general, evil vizier, heck before the core one dev had used him for a description as like a mercenary leader type.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-12T16:51:41-08:00","id":1367332,"title":"","content":"A sort of priest/warlord type, kinda using similar tactics to the Bodhisattva.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12314-grod_the_giant","name":"Grod_the_giant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12314_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-12T16:59:07-08:00","id":1367335,"title":"","content":"For whatever you think is in his wheel-house: throw 15-20-ish dice at it (or equivalent DV). If it's not in his wheel-house: 8-12 dice. Pick any set of Solar Charms (or equivalent effects) you think are appropriate for him, don't worry about prerequisites unless they also fit.<br /> <br /> I think nailing his personality in the encounter will be more important than the raw mechanics. I'd spend time thinking about what his goals, ties, and principles are and making some good intimacies for him over worrying about stats and other mechanics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12111-the_larz","name":"the_larz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-12T17:06:32-08:00","id":1367338,"title":"","content":"So, if you're not planning on having the Walker attack the party, and I assume they're not planning to attack him, then good news! This should be relatively easy. Not having to worry about combat stats should be a big, big decrease in difficulty. <br /> <br /> So, what you've got to work out are two main things: first, his basic social stats, and second, any charms he's got. The first is the easiest. Set his Resolve and Guile, give him Willpower, work out his dice pools for actions, and determine his Intimacies. For the numbers stuff, use the sample quick character writeups in the Antagonists chapter of the Core to get a sense of what numbers are appropriate. For a Deathlord, I'd compare stats with big spirits like Ahlat, Fakharu, and any of the 2nd-Circle demons. Then, since I think the Deathlords should be very impressive, the top tier of ghosts, I'd add at least 1 to static values, and 2 or more to action pools.<br /> <br /> For Intimacies, I'd create at <i>least</i> four, following the guidelines in the corebook about how they're broken down (at least one Defining, one Major, one negative, and one positive). But I find that NPCs intended for social encounters generally benefit from more Intimacies, since they give more &quot;hooks&quot; to hang social interactions on. My own rule of thumb is that there should be at least one Defining Intimacy, which should have at least two Major Intimacies that support it, each of which in turn should have an additional two <i>Minor</i> Intimacies supporting them. Then, if an NPC is supposed to be a very complex character with conflicting, or at least significantly complex motivations, I'll add a <i>second</i> Defining Intimacy, again supported by a chain of multiple lower-level Intimacies. If the second Defining is supposed to be in conflict with the first, all of the supporting Intimacies should be different, but if it's just intended to add some complexity to their characterization, it's okay for some of the lower-level ones to support multiple higher level ones. If I'm not planning on a more complex character, though, I'll probably still add another Major Intimacy and a single Minor Intimacy to support it, just to have an alternate route if all the &quot;main&quot; Intimacies get tapped out. <br /> <br /> Doing all that ensures that the NPC always has an Intimacy available to bolster their Resolve if someone tries to affect one of their higher-level Intimacies, and a second one available to enter a decision point if they overcome the first one. On the player-positive side, it also ensures that there's lots of ways for a PC to invoke the lesser Intimacies to get bonuses and enhance the interaction through roleplaying.<br /> <br /> Charms are going to need more work, I'm afraid. Again, I'd look at the existing QCs of equivalent or slightly lower power, and borrow from them. I'd pay particular attention to the Dead writeups here, since those charms will already have the closest flavor. But the Nephwrack, the closest to a Deathlord, only has one social charm, so you're probably still going to need to go further afield. Since this is intended for a primarily social encounter, I'd say you want at least three social charms detailed - one to enhance his ability to persuade, one to boost his Resolve, and one to help him determine others' Intimacies. Going through the social influence actions and coming up with a charm effect for each that you think he could use would not be a terrible idea, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-12T18:14:27-08:00","id":1367347,"title":"","content":"That's really helpful advice, Kelly-- thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12314-grod_the_giant","name":"Grod_the_giant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12314_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-18T12:56:46-08:00","id":1368787,"title":"","content":"Update: Here's what I'm thinking. (When I make QCs, I replace number-boosting charms with higher base die pools, and ignore motes in favor of running everything off willpower)<br /> <br /> <b>Essence </b>8, <b>Willpower</b> 8<br /> <b>Social Influence</b>: 18 dice<br /> <b>Deception</b>: 15 dice<br /> <b>Read Intentions</b>: 20 dice<br /> <br /> <b>Resolve </b>8<br /> <b>Guile </b>6<br /> <br /> Social Charms<ul><li><b>Penetrating Eyes (1wp): </b>Make a Read Intentions check against a target's Resolve. If you beat it, you learn all their intimacies.</li> <li><b>Mask of the Grave (1wp, Psyche): </b>When someone attempts a Read Intentions check against you, they see nothing but the despair of the grave. Roll dice equal to their successes on their roll against their Resolve. For every threshold success, they take 1 blunt damage.</li> <li><b>Manipulator (1wp)</b>: Once per scene, treat a Minor Intimacy as if it was a Major. Reset by instilling a new Major Intimacy.</li> <li><b>Hypnotic (1wp, Psyche): </b>Make a social influence roll against a target's Resolve. If you succeed, you may &quot;program&quot; them with one sentence per threshold success that they will speak at the time and place of your choosing. The speech doesn't strike anyone as unnatural unless they succeed on a Read Intentions check against your Guile. Instead of providing extra sentences, threshold successes can be added to the difficulty of this roll.</li> <li><b>Pervert (1wp, Psyche)</b>: Pick a Major or Minor Intimacy, either a target's or one of your own that's been instilled this scene, and make a social influence roll-- against the target's Resolve if against another person, or against the result of the Instill roll. On a success, change the Intimacy to something that better reflects the influence of the Neverborn.</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12314-grod_the_giant","name":"Grod_the_giant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12314_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-18T14:34:01-08:00","id":1368800,"title":"","content":"Those are some really, really powerful charms... and maybe that's okay?<br /> <br /> I'd suggest what you probably more want though is defensive social charms for him, especially if you're not intending him to do anything much to the party. What you don't want is them convincing him to, say, turn on the Neverborn, with just a few rolls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-18T16:15:45-08:00","id":1368815,"title":"","content":"So, wait, a Read Intentions just fails outright, <i>and</i> they take damage based on how many successes they rolled, for only one Willpower?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-18T19:58:20-08:00","id":1368842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1367327-um-i-might-need-stats-for-a-deathlord?p=1368815#post1368815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, wait, a Read Intentions just fails outright, <i>and</i> they take damage based on how many successes they rolled, for only one Willpower?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah.<br /> The fact it's turning an otherwise good roll back on the player and might be enough to kill some characters outright has a lot of potential to really piss someone off.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-18T20:54:23-08:00","id":1368850,"title":"","content":"There's certainly precedent for gaining benefits from your enemy's rolled successes, but directly damaging someone with their own roll in a way they can't actually avoid seems like dirty pool (<i>especially</i> when combined with making their roll automatically fail).<br /> <br /> I would suggest instead making that Charm: some kind of Guile increase, and if the read intentions action fails, the reader takes dice of unsoakable bashing damage equal to the number of successes by which they failed their roll. Or something like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-18T22:19:52-08:00","id":1368858,"title":"","content":"I think I largely agree with the Wizard - he needs a defensive charm to boost Resolve. And I agree with the others as well, Mask of the Grave is way too nasty. Success shouldn't be nearly so bad for players. <br /> <br /> Also, I don't think making them all cost just wp is a good idea. For one thing, wp is your most tight resource on most characters. If he uses all his charms just once, he'll only have 3 wp left over, and that's assuming he doesn't spend wp on anything <i>else</i>, like resisting the PCs' own social influence attempts. He should have a big, big mote pool - at Essence 8, a god would have 130 personal motes, and I think Deathlords are potent enough to deserve that much as well. I'd give most of those charms a mote cost. Wp costs are really for charms you only expect to use once or twice in a scene, whereas mote costs can be a bit freer. <br /> <br /> Another thing you might want to consider doing, since you have an Eclipse Caste in your group, is writing up at least one of his charms in a bit more detail, with a fair bit of flavor, and making it Eclipse-keyworded. That way, he has a bargaining chip he can use on the Eclipse: offer to teach them this nifty charm, in exchange for something. The Walker kind of has a &quot;warrior-poet&quot; thing going on, at least in his presentation in earlier editions, and a charm that plays with that could also work quite well with an Eclipse, particularly one interested in oral performance the way I'd expect a Silver-Voiced Nightingale stylist to be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-19T05:08:38-08:00","id":1368894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jefepato</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1367327-um-i-might-need-stats-for-a-deathlord?p=1368850#post1368850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's certainly precedent for gaining benefits from your enemy's rolled successes, but directly damaging someone with their own roll in a way they can't actually avoid seems like dirty pool (<i>especially</i> when combined with making their roll automatically fail).<br /> <br /> I would suggest instead making that Charm: some kind of Guile increase, and if the read intentions action fails, the reader takes dice of unsoakable bashing damage equal to the number of successes by which they failed their roll. Or something like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I also suspect the moment he deliberately hurts one of them for having the audacity to <i>look</i> <i>at him </i>most PC groups will be rolling join battle. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-19T06:48:29-08:00","id":1368916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1367327-um-i-might-need-stats-for-a-deathlord?p=1368894#post1368894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also suspect the moment he deliberately hurts one of them for having the audacity to <i>look</i> <i>at him </i>most PC groups will be rolling join battle. </div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, agreed.<br /> <br /> Presentation is very important with these kinds of encounters and damage is usually seen as overtly hostile.<br /> <br /> I'd be tempted to handle this narratively: on a successful Read Intentions they correctly divine his Intimacies as normal. It's just that his Intimacies are all creepy/horrifying/nihilistic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-19T07:00:16-08:00","id":1368918,"title":"","content":"I personally don't agree with just giving him giant dicepools and powering Charms just on WP. One thing I noticed when kludging together my own Deathlord stats was that some really high-level spirits have limited-applicability quasi-excellency Charms that allow them to buy dice or successes, like Ahlat's dice-adding being limited by his Initiative.That, and giving them big but not freakish dicepools, feels good to me.<br /> <br /> Mask of the Grave feels pretty rough, and I feel like it might be better to go about it differently. Maybe if someone beats his Guile with Read Intentions or Profile, he can use a Charm to reflexively and unnoticeably (or hard-to-noticeably) roll to Instill them with a Tie of horrified fascination, and if they rolled super well he can do it without cost.<br /> <br /> Y'all do y'all, but I know I as a player would not sit well with Mask of the Grave as written.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans","name":"Beans","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8026_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"472"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-19T07:02:13-08:00","id":1368919,"title":"","content":"I'm inclined to handle it more like Easily-Discarded Presence Method/Selfsame Master Procurer - on a <i>failed</i> Read Intentions, they see something grave and horrifying, letting him do a counter-influence to inspire terror.<br /> <br /> \u200bEDIT: Blast it, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8026_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8026\" data-vbnamecard=\"8026\">Beans</a>, when did you take a level in Ninja? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-19T08:18:49-08:00","id":1368935,"title":"","content":"Fair criticisms of Mask of the Grave. I'll change it to something more like TheCountAlucard's suggestion-- roll dice against their Resolve to inspire despair.<br /> <br /> As for a defensive charm... right before the game I added &quot;<b><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Nu (1 wp)</span></b><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">: Can pay an additional 1wp to use his Defining Intimacy in a decision point, even if he already used it initially.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kelly Pedersen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1367327-um-i-might-need-stats-for-a-deathlord?p=1368858#post1368858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, I don't think making them all cost just wp is a good idea. For one thing, wp is your most tight resource on most characters. If he uses all his charms just once, he'll only have 3 wp left over, and that's assuming he doesn't spend wp on anything <i>else</i>, like resisting the PCs' own social influence attempts. He should have a big, big mote pool - at Essence 8, a god would have 130 personal motes, and I think Deathlords are potent enough to deserve that much as well. I'd give most of those charms a mote cost. Wp costs are really for charms you only expect to use once or twice in a scene, whereas mote costs can be a bit freer.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beans</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1367327-um-i-might-need-stats-for-a-deathlord?p=1368918#post1368918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I personally don't agree with just giving him giant dicepools and powering Charms just on WP. One thing I noticed when kludging together my own Deathlord stats was that some really high-level spirits have limited-applicability quasi-excellency Charms that allow them to buy dice or successes, like Ahlat's dice-adding being limited by his Initiative.That, and giving them big but not freakish dicepools, feels good to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a practice I started with combat enemies-- like I mentioned, this was the first time they ran into something with social charms-- where I started doing it mostly for my own sanity. I ran an Abyssal enemy earlier in the game with a bunch of Charms pulled from the Soulfarer evocation list and Lanaya's Abyssal homebrew, and trying to keep track of everything was awful. Idiosyncratic dice tricks are fun for PCs, but not so much as a GM. I've started cranking up dice pools to simulate a the steady burn of number-boosting Charms, and limiting <i>actual </i>Charms to ones that do new stuff.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kelly Pedersen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1367327-um-i-might-need-stats-for-a-deathlord?p=1368858#post1368858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another thing you might want to consider doing, since you have an Eclipse Caste in your group, is writing up at least one of his charms in a bit more detail, with a fair bit of flavor, and making it Eclipse-keyworded. That way, he has a bargaining chip he can use on the Eclipse: offer to teach them this nifty charm, in exchange for something. The Walker kind of has a &quot;warrior-poet&quot; thing going on, at least in his presentation in earlier editions, and a charm that plays with that could also work quite well with an Eclipse, particularly one interested in oral performance the way I'd expect a Silver-Voiced Nightingale stylist to be.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like that idea-- unfortunately, the Eclipse player wound up not being able to make the session. Fortunately the Twilight proved delightfully vulnerable to temptation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12314-grod_the_giant","name":"Grod_the_giant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12314_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-19T09:14:44-08:00","id":1368948,"title":"","content":"Since lots of people already gave practical and sensible suggestions and criticisms - and, if i'm understanding the OP's last post correctly, the encounter with the Deathlord already happened - i'll thrown in some delirious &amp; capricious ones instead.<br /> <br /> I would work with the Nephwrack QC and add bits and pieces for color and evocative theming as appropriate. Ess5 is fine for a first showing, one can always bring the Ess6+ real mojo in later encounters if need be. ST and players having fun with each encounter involving it is more important than optimizing or fitting the NPC in any canon power tier or whatever.<br /> <br /> Speaking of themes &amp; imagery, the deathlord is called Walker in <i><b>Darkness</b></i>, so that already gives us some imagery of darkness &amp; shadows to mess with for a start. Insomnia or sleepwalking (possession by the Whispers?), with some dream-like weirdness imagery, could also go well with the <b><i>Walker </i></b>in Darkness part.<br /> Ebon Shadow Style can go greatly with that, Mists of Eventide, Silent Words of Dreams &amp; Nightmares, Impenetrable Veil of Night, Shadows of the Ancient Past for spells, control spells, might too. Also, we are speaking of a Deathlord, gank the rules, let him have <b>all </b>of those as control spells and the PCs suffer before the utter messed up fruits of dealing with someone who sinergizes all these effects. For extra nastiness, add a modified version of the <i><b>Miracles of Shadow and Chaos</b></i> merit (from the Scarred by Nightmares shaping ritual), that works from its own mists/darkness instead of the Wyld.<br /> Other stuff you might want to look into from the core are the charms <i><b>Night-Black Carapace</b></i> (Alveua), <i><b>Handmaid of Dark Fates</b></i> &amp; <b><i>Hundred-Faced Shadow</i></b> (Mara) for extra tricks &amp; inspiration.<br /> <br /> \u200bCreatures of the night could fit too - and offer a gothic/vampiric twist on the image of the serene priest/holy person surrounded by becalmed beasts. If you want to go in that direction, messing with some survival charms related to animal taming or familiar-boosting might give you ideas too. A retouched version of Alveua's <b><i>Plague of Shining Insects </i></b>would also go well with that, imho.<br /> <br /> Completely making up stuff as i go along won't deny, but having lots of fun with it anyway.<br /> Hope it is of some use for anyone or at least makes for an entertaining read. See ya.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 02-19-2020, 11:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-19T09:26:39-08:00","id":1368950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grod_the_giant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1367327-um-i-might-need-stats-for-a-deathlord?p=1368935#post1368935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a practice I started with combat enemies-- like I mentioned, this was the first time they ran into something with social charms-- where I started doing it mostly for my own sanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's fair, keeping track of a big essence pool can be a huge pain, even when things don't move as fast as they do in combat. <br /> <br /> Still, though, I don't think using all willpower costs is the way to do it. Social influence is heavily dependent on willpower expenditures, and saving wp for resisting stuff is pretty important. Also, wp can be spent to just add a bonus success to an NPC's die roll, which can make a big difference too. What I'd suggest instead is to divide the motepool by 10 or so, and just have all his charms cost a multiple of 10, and just track it that way. So he might have 13 &quot;decamotes&quot;, and one charm might cost 1 decamote, another more expensive one might cost 2, and the most expensive costs 3. That would make the bookkeeping about as simple as wp tracking, but not use up wp.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-19T13:30:07-08:00","id":1369002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1367327-um-i-might-need-stats-for-a-deathlord?p=1368916#post1368916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd be tempted to handle this narratively: on a successful Read Intentions they correctly divine his Intimacies as normal. It's just that his Intimacies are all creepy/horrifying/nihilistic.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've got to say, I actually think the concept that a Deathlord can make their soul grim enough that to look upon it and try to understand it can result in actual harm to a person is really neat as an idea for what makes something being a Deathlord have metaphysical weight that one might expect of such an entity.<br /> <br /> I do agree that the mechanics might need some revision, and as far as playing it out goes... I think perhaps one might Storytell the thing coming through in stages. A character tries to read the Deathlord, they come to the threshold of that Essence, and the ghost looks at them and says &quot;are you sure you want to do that&quot;? It can get some of the point across without damaging the player, and offers them the choice about whether or not they want to go ahead with it.<br /> <br /> But with that in mind, I'd say that the player ought to get something for their trouble; if a bit of understanding of the Deathlord can cause harm, maybe have them actually get some understanding out of it.<br /> <br /> Maybe divide the ideas; one Charm to block off attempts to read, one to make those that work a vector for a bit of harm. In the latter case, maybe it costs the Deathlord that they don't get to apply their Guile, or at least take a hit to it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-19T13:58:19-08:00","id":1369013,"title":"","content":"There's some Lunar charms that strip willpower and even instil derangements when you fail to Read their Intentions. That seems like something you could use as a model.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-19T15:34:20-08:00","id":1369035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1367327-um-i-might-need-stats-for-a-deathlord?p=1369002#post1369002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've got to say, I actually think the concept that a Deathlord can make their soul grim enough that to look upon it and try to understand it can result in actual harm to a person is really neat as an idea for what makes something being a Deathlord have metaphysical weight that one might expect of such an entity.<br /> <br /> I do agree that the mechanics might need some revision, and as far as playing it out goes... I think perhaps one might Storytell the thing coming through in stages. A character tries to read the Deathlord, they come to the threshold of that Essence, and the ghost looks at them and says &amp;quot;are you sure you want to do that&amp;quot;? It can get some of the point across without damaging the player, and offers them the choice about whether or not they want to go ahead with it.<br /> <br /> But with that in mind, I'd say that the player ought to get something for their trouble; if a bit of understanding of the Deathlord can cause harm, maybe have them actually get some understanding out of it.<br /> <br /> Maybe divide the ideas; one Charm to block off attempts to read, one to make those that work a vector for a bit of harm. In the latter case, maybe it costs the Deathlord that they don't get to apply their Guile, or at least take a hit to it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I terms of high concept, I agree completely. It's great design space and a neat idea. Very thematic.<br /> <br /> In terms of OP wanting a social interaction (3E's social system being based entirely around discivering and manipulating Intimacies) that doesn't turn into a TPK combat encounter... no.<br /> <br /> &quot;I Read Intentions so I can actually do something in this Social Encounter!&quot;<br /> &quot;Do you really want to do that?&quot;<br /> &quot;... Yes?&quot;<br /> &quot;Aaaand you're dead.&quot;<br /> &quot;Kyle is dead? I draw my daiklave!&quot;<br /> &quot;Do you really want to do that?&quot;<br /> <br /> I'm not saying it can't be done, but I wouldn't want to run it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-19T17:36:36-08:00","id":1369058,"title":"","content":"I must say that I also find the concept of Deathlord dealing literal damage when you try to look into his soul immensely cool, so I'd advice to keep it to some extent. I'd also make it depend upon player's choice. I'd imagine something along the following lines:<br /> <br /> When you try to understand his motives, you first narrate how they feel this dark an ancient impenetrable presence. You roll for read intentions. If you succeed, you choose: either get an intention of Storyteller's choice, or what you was initially trying to read. If it's the latter, you are subject to Enviromental Hazard, 5B/round, Diff 7, opposed with [Wits + Integrity] roll. Each round, you can keep reading intentions with the difficulty lowering by 1 each turn (it gets easier!), but you are exposed to the hazard (possibly the hazard becomes more harmful). If you stop reading intentions, you are no more exposed to damage, but you can no more read his intentions during this scene.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13416,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","user":"Lanic","date":". 02-19-2020, 08:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","name":"Lanic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-19T19:25:04-08:00","id":1369081,"title":"","content":"Suggestions to try and split the difference on Mask of the Grave. The deeper one stares into the Void, the more the Void stares back into the observer. The character gains no benefit from their Read Intentions roll, indeed each threshold success costs the character one point of temporary willpower. If this is more than the character's reserve of temporary willpower, the deficit converts to Bashing Damage. (Potentially also having a once-per-session limit on Walker's use of this Charm)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25940-arykaran","name":"ArykAran","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25940_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-19T19:26:02-08:00","id":1369082,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArykAran</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1367327-um-i-might-need-stats-for-a-deathlord?p=1369081#post1369081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Suggestions to try and split the difference on Mask of the Grave. The deeper one stares into the Void, the more the Void stares back into the observer. The character gains no benefit from their Read Intentions roll, indeed each threshold success costs the character one point of temporary willpower. If this is more than the character's reserve of temporary willpower, the deficit converts to Bashing Damage. (Potentially also having a once-per-session limit on Walker's use of this Charm)</div> </div> </div> </div>That's even more powerful!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25764-vwllss-trnt-prncss","name":"vwllss trnt prncss","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-19T19:39:22-08:00","id":1369085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArykAran</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1367327-um-i-might-need-stats-for-a-deathlord?p=1369081#post1369081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Suggestions to try and split the difference on Mask of the Grave. The deeper one stares into the Void, the more the Void stares back into the observer. The character gains no benefit from their Read Intentions roll, indeed each threshold success costs the character one point of temporary willpower. If this is more than the character's reserve of temporary willpower, the deficit converts to Bashing Damage. (Potentially also having a once-per-session limit on Walker's use of this Charm)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I would suggest a little &quot;easter egg&quot; of sorts in that &quot;staring at the Void&quot; let's the PC pick between <b><i>learning Whispers as a training effect</i></b> <b>or</b> spending willpower &amp;/or taking damage to purge one's soul &amp; memory of the unspeakable revelations. Alternately, the PC may choose to suffer a derangement if the damage might be enough to incapacitate or kill it, in a riff of the rule about accepting a crippling injury/losing a limb, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 02-19-2020, 10:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}